    "detailed_movement_en": "1. Starting Setup: Sit on an exercise ball with your feet flat on the ground and your back resting against an incline bench.\n\n2. Initial Execution: Hold a cable handle in one hand and position your arm at a 90-degree angle with your elbow bent.\n\n3. Primary Phase & Control: Press the cable handle forward and upward, extending your arm fully.\n\n4. Controlled Return: Pause for a moment at the top, then slowly lower the cable handle back to the starting position.\n\n5. Continuity & Repetitions: Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch to the other arm.",
