    "detailed_movement_en": "1. Starting Setup: Sit on an exercise ball with your feet flat on the ground and your back straight.\n\n2. Initial Execution: Hold a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing your body and your arms fully extended.\n\n3. Primary Phase & Control: Keeping your upper arms stationary, exhale and curl one dumbbell up towards your shoulder while keeping your palm facing your body.\n\n4. Controlled Return: Continue to raise the dumbbell until your biceps are fully contracted and the dumbbell is at shoulder level.\n\n5. Step 5: Hold the contracted position for a brief pause as you squeeze your biceps.\n\n6. Step 6: Inhale and slowly lower the dumbbell back to the starting position.\n\n7. Step 7: Repeat the movement with the opposite arm.\n\n8. Continuity & Repetitions: Continue alternating arms for the desired number of repetitions.",
